Given equation is $x^{2}+x+1=0\Rightarrow \quad x=\omega$ and $x=\omega^{2}$
Case I : When $x=\omega$
Then
$\sum_{n=1}^{6}\left[x^{n}+\frac{1}{x^{n}}\right]^{2}=\sum_{n=1}^{6}\left[\omega^{n}+\omega^{2 n}\right]^{2}\left[\because \frac{1}{\omega}=\omega^{2}\right]=\left(\omega+\omega^{2}\right)^{2}+\left(\omega^{2}+\omega^{4}\right)^{2}+\left(\omega^{3}+\omega^{6}\right)^{2}+\left(\omega^{4}+\omega^{8}\right)^{2}+\left(\omega^{5}+\omega^{10}\right)^{2}+\left(\omega^{6}+\omega^{12}\right)^{2}\begin{array}{r}
=(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(2)^{2}+(-1)^{2} \\
+(-1)^{2}+(2)^{2}=12
